CLAIM = for N in {3, 4}, every J >= 300 and every d_L = -1 row of TRICK_DLM1_v1_4_r1 (895634f5) of kind <kind> (D3B for class D3, D4A for D4, D4MA for D4M), with a-hat = a = S'^-1 w-hat (so <u, a-hat> = 1 and <a-hat, X_1 u> = 1) and X_e, X_f the single centred bond operators of OPERATOR_SINGLE_<kind>: q_e = ||Q0 X_e* a-hat|| <= ||X_e* a-hat|| <= N*_QE_HI_<kind> and q_f = ||Q0 X_f* a-hat|| <= ||X_f* a-hat|| <= N*_QF_HI_<kind>, for every centre in the row's box (v3's ce and cf fields). Bond e is t for every kind; bond f is bb (D3B) or b (D4A, D4MA). N*_QF_HI_D4MA already holds the J-uniform lambda_h/lambda_0 factor, so the reader must not apply it again; no other key carries a lambda factor.
KEYMAP_D3B = QE N*_QE_HI_D3B (bond t) ; QF N*_QF_HI_D3B (bond bb) (rows of class D3)
KEYMAP_D4A = QE N*_QE_HI_D4A (bond t) ; QF N*_QF_HI_D4A (bond b) (rows of class D4)
KEYMAP_D4MA = QE N*_QE_HI_D4MA (bond t) ; QF N*_QF_HI_D4MA (bond b) (rows of class D4M)
OBJECTS = as in the lemma notes (6d0864e5 sect. 1, 8aadb7e8 sect. 1) and v3's OPERATOR_D3, OPERATOR_D4, OPERATOR_D4M: Z = K^(1/2) V^(1/2), T = Z Z*, Th = Z* Z = V^(1/2) K V^(1/2); ||Z||_H = lambda_0^(1/2) and ||Th||_H = lambda_0 (T and Th have the same top eigenvalue on H); G_t = V^(1/2) (K_t - c_t K) V^(1/2) with ||G_t||_H <= (A + |c_t|) lambda_0 (F4), G_bb likewise; M is multiplication by xi_b - c_b; Z* a-hat = (lambda_0/<u,w>) V^(1/2) 1 with ||V^(1/2) 1|| = v_0 and 1 + tau^2 = lambda_0 v_0^2/<u,w>^2 (B6); every vector below lies in H (Z, Th, G and M commute with the diagonal O(N) action, and V^(1/2) 1 is invariant)
OPERATOR_SINGLE_D3B = the D3 frame (w = 3; t = gap-0 top, bb = gap-1 bottom) with the other bond's insertion removed: lambda_0^3 X_t = Z G_t Th Z*, lambda_0^3 X_bb = Z Th G_bb Z*
OPERATOR_SINGLE_D4A = the D4 frame (w = 2; t = gap-0 top, b = column-0 MB vertical): lambda_0^2 X_t = Z G_t Z* (M -> 1), lambda_0^2 X_b = Z M Th Z* (G_t -> Th)
OPERATOR_SINGLE_D4MA = the D4M frame (w = 2; t = gap-0 top, b = column-1 MB vertical): lambda_0^2 X_t = Z G_t Z* (M -> 1), lambda_0^2 X_b = Z Th M Z* (G_t -> Th)
FORMULA_D3B = Lemma B's B3 and B5 with one G replaced by Th: ||X_t* a-hat|| <= ||Z||_H ||Th||_H ||G_t||_H ||Z* a-hat||/lambda_0^3 = (A + |c_t|) (1 + tau^2)^(1/2), and ||X_bb* a-hat|| <= (A + |c_bb|) (1 + tau^2)^(1/2); sups at the box's largest |c|; no lambda factor
FORMULA_D4A = bond t: X_t* a-hat = (lambda_0/<u,w>) Z h/lambda_0^2 with h = G_t V^(1/2) 1, ||h|| <= (A + |c_t|) lambda_0 v_0 (A-D4M's M1), so ||X_t* a-hat|| <= (A + |c_t|) (1 + tau^2)^(1/2); bond b: X_b* = Z Th M Z*/lambda_0^2 and X_b* a-hat = (lambda_0/<u,w>) Z Th f/lambda_0^2 with f = M V^(1/2) 1, ||f|| = v_0 E_1(c_b)^(1/2) (A3), so ||X_b* a-hat|| <= (1 + tau^2)^(1/2) E_1(c_b)^(1/2) <= (1 + tau^2)^(1/2) ((A - c_b)^2 + A^2)^(1/2) for c_b < J + A (A5, A6); sup at the box's smallest c_b (c_b <= A on the box); no lambda factor
FORMULA_D4MA = bond t: as D4A's (the same X_t); bond b: X_b* = Z M Th Z*/lambda_0^2 and X_b* a-hat = (lambda_0/<u,w>) Z M h1/lambda_0^2 with h1 = Th V^(1/2) 1, ||h1|| <= lambda_0 v_0, and ||Z M||_H <= ||Z M||_HS,H <= (A2 + c_b^2 A0)^(1/2) lambda_h^(1/2) for c_b >= 0 (A-D4M's M2, Lemma D4 of 1340a52c), so ||X_b* a-hat|| <= (1 + tau^2)^(1/2) (A2 + c_b^2 A0)^(1/2) (lambda_h/lambda_0)^(1/2), with lambda_h/lambda_0 <= 1/(N*_I_FREE_LO N*_RQH_LO) (TAU_D3B_v1's J-uniform fallback, as in TRICK_DLM1's Q_HI_D4MA); sup at the box's largest c_b
FORMULA_VALUES = in exact rationals from v3's A, A2, A0_HI and boxes and TAU_D3B_v1's TAU_HI, I_FREE_LO and RQH_LO; each value the smallest 12-significant-digit decimal whose square is at or above the formula's square at the sup corner (C-QEF)
CHECK_JOINT = per kind and N, QE^2 QF^2 = Q^2 (1 + tau^2) exactly, with Q^2 the joint lemma's square at the same corners, and Q^2 at most TRICK_DLM1_v1_4_r1's N*_Q_HI_<kind>^2 and within 1e-10 of it (C-JOINT)
NOTE_SCOPE = crude forms (the review 6e38bd40 sect. (a): a crude bound will do for type A; the approval 2026-11-09T00:21Z allows crude for every kind). TRICK_DLM1_v1_4_r1 lists the row N4 D3 (-1,2) as OPEN for its joint q; the single-bond keys hold for it as for every row
NOTE_LAMBDA = N*_QF_HI_D4MA uses the exact ratio 1/(N*_I_FREE_LO N*_RQH_LO) of TAU_D3B_v1's decimals; N*_LAMBDA_RATIO_HI is its 12-digit upper end, written for reference only
